# One Knowledge Commons License v1.0

OKCL-1.0 · Copyright © 2026 One Systems Inc.

Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person or entity
obtaining a copy of this data and associated documentation files (the
"Knowledge"), to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, and create
derivative works of the Knowledge, subject to the following conditions:

## 1. Visible Attribution

(a) The copyright notice, this permission notice, and the meta block
contained in each Knowledge file (including source, url, and license fields)
shall be included in all copies or substantial portions of the Knowledge.

(b) Attribution to "One Systems Inc. (withone.ai)" must be preserved in any
derivative work, including but not limited to documentation, applications,
knowledge bases, and datasets derived from the Knowledge.

(c) Any system, application, or user interface that surfaces actions,
integrations, or capabilities derived from the Knowledge to end users or AI
agents must include human-visible attribution stating "Integration knowledge
by One (withone.ai)" or a substantially similar notice. Where no user
interface exists, machine-readable attribution must be included in API
responses or agent-accessible metadata.

(d) The attribution obligations in this section propagate to all downstream
recipients and derivative works. No sublicense, fork, modification, or
redistribution may remove, obscure, or fail to propagate these attribution
requirements.

## 2. Schema Integrity

The meta fields in Knowledge files, including source, url, license, and
maintained_by, must not be removed, altered, or obscured in any distribution
of the Knowledge.

The $schema reference must not be modified to point to an alternative schema
authority.

## 3. Anti-Extraction

(a) You may not use the Knowledge, or any substantial portion or derivative
thereof, to build, train, populate, improve, or supplement a competing
integration knowledge base, action registry, API schema repository, or any
structured dataset designed to enable AI agents or automated systems to
discover, understand, or execute actions on third-party platforms.

(b) You may not use the Knowledge as training data, fine-tuning data,
retrieval-augmentation data, or any other input to artificial intelligence
or machine learning systems for the purpose of generating or deriving a
competing knowledge base as described in Section 3(a).

(c) If the Knowledge is used as input to AI or machine learning systems for
any permitted purpose, the model provider or developer must include "One
Systems Inc. (withone.ai)" in any public-facing training data attribution,
data provenance documentation, or model card disclosures. AI systems that
generate outputs substantially derived from the Knowledge should attribute
the source when feasible.

(d) This section applies regardless of the degree of modification,
transformation, or abstraction applied to the Knowledge.

## 4. Commercial Licensing Threshold

(a) Any entity whose commercial offering includes, as a primary or material
component, integration infrastructure, API aggregation, agent tooling
platforms, agent orchestration services, or integration-knowledge services,
and whose consolidated annual revenue (including revenue of all affiliates
and parent entities) exceeds One Million United States Dollars
($1,000,000 USD), must obtain a commercial license from One Systems Inc.
prior to any use of the Knowledge. Contact license@withone.ai for commercial
licensing.

(b) For purposes of this section, "material component" means that the
entity's product or service relies on integration knowledge, API schemas,
action definitions, or similar structured data to enable AI agents, automated
workflows, or end users to interact with third-party platforms, and this
capability constitutes a significant part of the product's value
proposition — whether marketed as integration infrastructure, agent tooling,
agent orchestration, workflow automation, or under any other description.

(c) This threshold does not apply to entities using the Knowledge solely to
power integrations within their own end-user products, internal systems, or
private deployments that are not offered to third parties as integration or
agent infrastructure.

(d) Revenue is measured on a trailing twelve-month basis. If an entity
exceeds the threshold, it must obtain a commercial license within 90 days of
crossing the threshold.

## 5. No Enclosure

You may not restrict access to the Knowledge, or substantial derivatives
thereof, behind authentication, API keys, paywalls, or rate limits for the
purpose of selling, monetizing, or commercially distributing access to the
Knowledge as a standalone data product or hosted service.

## 6. Share-Alike for Derivatives

(a) If you distribute, publish, or make publicly available any derivative
work based on the Knowledge, you must release such derivative work under this
same license (OKCL-1.0) or a later version published by One Systems Inc.

(b) Derivative works include but are not limited to: modified Knowledge
files, new Knowledge files created using the same schema, translated or
reformatted versions of the Knowledge, and datasets substantially derived
from the Knowledge.

(c) This requirement does not apply to end-user applications or products
that merely consume or embed the Knowledge without redistributing the
Knowledge files themselves.

## 7. Community Contributions

Contributions to the Knowledge are accepted under the terms of this license.
Contributors retain copyright to their contributions but grant One Systems
Inc. and all downstream users a perpetual, irrevocable, royalty-free license
to use, modify, and distribute the contributions under these same terms.

## 8. Patent Peace

If you initiate any patent claim, lawsuit, or other patent enforcement action
against One Systems Inc. or any other licensee alleging that the Knowledge
(or any portion thereof) infringes a patent, your rights under this license
terminate immediately and automatically.

## 9. Termination and Cure

(a) Any violation of this license automatically terminates your rights
under it.

(b) If you cure the violation within 30 days of becoming aware of it, your
rights are reinstated retroactively, provided this is your first violation.

(c) A second violation permanently and irrevocably terminates your rights
under this license.

## 10. No Warranty

The Knowledge is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or
implied, including but not limited to the warranties of merchantability,
fitness for a particular purpose and noninfringement. In no event shall One
Systems Inc. be liable for any claim, damages or other liability, whether in
an action of contract, tort or otherwise, arising from, out of or in
connection with the Knowledge or the use or other dealings in the Knowledge.

